[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The one-node-per-file layout has no executable guard

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SDOC-LAYOUT-CHECK
TITLE: The one-node-per-file layout has no executable guard
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
A check over docs/**/*.sdoc and **/.sdoc/*.sdoc asserting three things per
file: exactly one node tag, a basename equal to the node's UID lowercased plus
.sdoc, and a document TITLE equal to the node's TITLE. Wired into flake.nix
beside strictdoc-cycle-check and strictdoc-fp-check, so it runs in nix flake
check.

A fourth assertion belongs here too, once the layout half is working: the
backlog pair. A node at DEPTH sketch must carry Backlogged_In to its own plan's
register, and a node above sketch must not carry one. The two halves are the
same check because they are the same failure -- somebody filing without
attaching, or grooming without detaching -- and the DEPTH == sketch query is
what makes it decidable without a second source of truth.

None of the four is enforced by anything today. StrictDoc parses a multi-node
document, a mismatched filename and a divergent document title without
complaint, and it does not know what Backlogged_In means, so all of it holds
only for as long as every session remembers it.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
INV-GUARDS-MUST-EXECUTE is the reason this is a node rather than a paragraph in
the skill. A layout rule that only prose enforces decays the first time a
session writes a node the way it wrote them before the carve, and the failure is
silent: the graph still exports, the edges still resolve, and only the context
cost goes back up.

Cheap to write because the carve already proved every predicate. The
verification pass over all 161 files compared basename to UID and document TITLE
to node TITLE and found zero exceptions, and the backlog wiring was verified as
a set equality in both directions across all 81 sketch nodes. The check starts
green, so its first red is a real regression rather than a backlog of existing
violations.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Filed 2026-08-27 by the carve session. Not built in that session because adding
a flake check is implementation work and the carve was a migration.

The natural home is checks/strictdoc-layout-check.nix, alongside the eight
existing strictdoc-* checks. Note that a runCommandLocal derivation sets
allowSubstitutes = false and would re-execute on every flake check rather than
being fetched from the cache.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MECH-BACKLOG-STRICTDOC-TOOLING
  ROLE: Backlogged_In
